                  <th>Viewing Surface</th>
                  <th>Aspect Ratio</th>
                  <th>Pixel Dimensions</th>
                  <th>Where It Appears &amp; Cropping Behavior</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Fullscreen Reels Tab</strong></td>
                  <td><strong>9:16 Vertical</strong></td>
                  <td>1080 × 1920 px</td>
                  <td>Full vertical screen in the dedicated Reels feed and Stories viewer. Subject to top, right, and bottom UI obstruction.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Home Feed Scroll</strong></td>
                  <td><strong>4:5 Portrait</strong></td>
                  <td>1080 × 1350 px</td>
                  <td>In the scrollable home feed, Instagram trims 285px off the top and 285px off the bottom. Critical text must sit inside this 1350px window.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Profile Grid Thumbnail</strong></td>
                  <td><strong>1:1 Square</strong></td>
                  <td>1080 × 1080 px</td>
                  <td>In your 3-column account profile grid, Instagram cuts 420px off the top and 420px off the bottom, displaying only the exact center square.</td>
