            <li><strong>Optimal Font Size:</strong> At full 1080 × 1920 resolution, primary text hooks should measure between 60pt and 80pt, while ongoing subtitle text should stay between 44pt and 54pt. Anything smaller than 40pt becomes difficult to read on 6-inch mobile screens without straining.</li>
            <li><strong>Word Chunking (1 to 3 Words Per Screen):</strong> Research shows fast, synchronized 1 to 3 word subtitle chunks maintain dramatically higher visual momentum than multi-line sentence paragraphs. Keep animated subtitle cards concise so viewers absorb the message in real time without cognitive friction.</li>
            <li><strong>Clean, Heavy Sans-Serif Typefaces:</strong> Choose bold, high-legibility typefaces such as Montserrat, Futura Bold, Inter, or The Bold Font. Avoid delicate script, thin handwriting, or overly condensed typefaces that blur during mobile video compression.</li>
            <li><strong>Strategic Color Accents:</strong> Use high-contrast color highlights (such as vibrant yellow `#FACC15` or electric green `#22C55E` against white text) on core emotional trigger words. This guides the viewer's eye and emphasizes the central takeaway of each sentence.</li>
